{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/141374-tokens","id":141374,"title":"Tokens","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-05-18T01:45:27-07:00","id":141374,"title":"Tokens","content":"So, I'm curious. Are there rules for creating new Tokens listed anywhere? Can Changelings even create there own magic items?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2875-jamesfhj","name":"JamesFHJ","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-18T02:08:16-07:00","id":141412,"title":"","content":"Rites of Spring has rules for Hedgespinning, which allows Changelings to create new items from a mixture of tangible and intangible items. It's pretty flexible, my players adore it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-18T03:03:51-07:00","id":141423,"title":"","content":"There are ways to create Tokens. There are no rules. Hedgespinning is nice but Token creation would have been nicer considering how that system works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-18T05:22:34-07:00","id":141470,"title":"","content":"A changeling can &quot;create&quot; a Token by burying an item in the Hedge, waiting for weeks, months, or years, and hoping. The Hedge does all the magical stuff, though, so the one who buries it has no real control. <br /> <br /> Alternately, you can pick up the &quot;Token Maker&quot; merit and get a bunch of successes on Crafts rolls. <br /> <br /> As for how to devise the powers and weaknesses of said tokens, that's unfortunately free-form. I know that the Camarilla fanclub has a set of token-creation rules, and others probably have similar, but to the best of my knowledge there's nothing official.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-18T15:42:35-07:00","id":141888,"title":"","content":"So I just read the Hedgespun Tokens stuff from Rites of Spring? So awesome. I actually like these better than regular tokens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2875-jamesfhj","name":"JamesFHJ","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-18T19:14:16-07:00","id":141995,"title":"","content":"At the highest levels of Wyrd, some changelings unconsciously create tokens from interacting with objects of the real world. (Equinox Road, Tokenmaster merit)<br /> <br /> They really don't have any control over what things become tokens, or what powers and catches the token will be able to manifest. I imagine that becoming an unwitting vector for the dissemination of Arcadian madness to be pretty damaging to Clarity. It is also not inconceivable that these tokens have more than just a sympathetic link to the changeling that imbued them through proximity to their bloated Wyrd. <br /> <br /> Cause when it comes to tokens, there is always a catch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1996-firefly-night","name":"Firefly Night","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}